[{:db/id "q-117666/selection/4f1ffa38d73b18554a47d8d9cea1139f02bb33ce8900fc955ea927ce75c224e3" :answer/id #uuid "9ea249d8-30d5-5804-84dd-69702ba7be1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "62" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117666/selection/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" :answer/id #uuid "2d5e053e-2fd0-5b0e-bf97-ca02452a3d11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117666/selection/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" :answer/id #uuid "84d8ab6b-d244-5fb6-bd0d-7bd83a787197" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117666/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer/id #uuid "48686f43-375c-5027-b3aa-9095101538ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117666/selection/842947b00d8ffc5745884eed061ea57d57affe318d15d13be5c3612b41e13326" :answer/id #uuid "4a1ea743-cf10-507e-ac95-e3e545c984ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "84" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117666/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "826651a7-01f6-5aa1-8623-1d556360809b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117666/selection/842947b00d8ffc5745884eed061ea57d57affe318d15d13be5c3612b41e13326" :answer-field/choices ["q-117666/selection/4f1ffa38d73b18554a47d8d9cea1139f02bb33ce8900fc955ea927ce75c224e3" "q-117666/selection/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" "q-117666/selection/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" "q-117666/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" "q-117666/selection/842947b00d8ffc5745884eed061ea57d57affe318d15d13be5c3612b41e13326"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117666" :question/id #uuid "bebd9b42-4c15-5a4c-bcc4-3722f4a7881d" :question/math-academy-id "q-117666" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of \n${\\int }_{-5}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}7-3x, & x<-1 \\\\ 10, & x\\ge -1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-5}^{-1}(7-3x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}10\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(7x-3\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}){|}_{-5}^{-1}+10x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =[7(-1)-3\\frac{(-1)^{2}}{2}-7(-5)+3\\frac{(-5)^{2}}{2}]+10[(1)-(-1)] \\\\  & =[28+36]+10[2] \\\\  & =64+20 \\\\  & =84.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-117666/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec980fcb-97ed-5c60-94de-0521d9d7df27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117666"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342011/field-1/f48b848c0ba9eb972a6ecdade8ce516585f3a0e3b5dbeab089775adb9307dc15" :answer/id #uuid "35db7ba8-10f3-5b28-9231-9281b1b81746" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342011/field-1/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer/id #uuid "d69c42e2-62a4-585d-9fe1-e50bb4e78dfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342011/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "368004ae-0c60-520c-ae06-2727af4c31ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342011/field-1/f48b848c0ba9eb972a6ecdade8ce516585f3a0e3b5dbeab089775adb9307dc15" :answer-field/choices ["q-342011/field-1/f48b848c0ba9eb972a6ecdade8ce516585f3a0e3b5dbeab089775adb9307dc15" "q-342011/field-1/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342011" :question/id #uuid "eac685d5-1f91-5a31-b64f-648b8efa1ec8" :question/math-academy-id "q-342011" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}, & x<1, \\\\ -2x+3, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{1}^{3}(-2x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}){|}_{-1}^{1}\\,+\\,(-{x}^{2}+3x){|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3}-(\\frac{1}{3}(-1)^{3})]\\,+\\,[-{3}^{2}+3(3)-(-{1}^{2}+3(1))] \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}-(-\\frac{1}{3})]\\,+\\,[0-2] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342011/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec980fcb-97ed-5c60-94de-0521d9d7df27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342011"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117669/selection/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" :answer/id #uuid "661af475-d92a-5fa0-a02c-051a8ea83cce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117669/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "366bc398-d197-5005-85ec-47cddefb648e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117669/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225" :answer/id #uuid "89e4c37f-f88c-57b1-9263-b4a9fb440858" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117669/selection/0f4c4dd728824ee19d0a7bf37e750d49d803dbb84e7cbc9edb64740edc2f53d0" :answer/id #uuid "77aaf520-58b8-502a-8c99-aa6ccf2212ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117669/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "e921000f-4906-542d-85d7-1f44c483694a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117669/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eeef0fcf-c965-51e2-b18c-4f01c8f232f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117669/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225" :answer-field/choices ["q-117669/selection/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" "q-117669/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-117669/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225" "q-117669/selection/0f4c4dd728824ee19d0a7bf37e750d49d803dbb84e7cbc9edb64740edc2f53d0" "q-117669/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117669" :question/id #uuid "eaf2bfbd-fd1d-5fe9-ac11-0df52f6066be" :question/math-academy-id "q-117669" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of \n${\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}1-{x}^{2}, & x<0 \\\\ 2x+1, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}){|}_{-2}^{0}+({x}^{2}+x){|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[(0)-\\frac{(0)^{3}}{3}-(-2)+\\frac{(-2)^{3}}{3}]+[(2)^{2}+2-(0)^{2}-(0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}+6 \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-117669/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec980fcb-97ed-5c60-94de-0521d9d7df27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117669"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342008/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "c3b6eb8b-d7e6-5633-8a80-2e6304a96ebb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342008/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa20d964-5c3d-55e5-ad89-be71a77cb196" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342008/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-342008/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342008" :question/id #uuid "a300e381-0c39-5f73-b474-493430914749" :question/math-academy-id "q-342008" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x+2, & x<0, \\\\ -2x+1, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-4}^{0}(\\frac{1}{2}x+2)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{0}^{3}(-2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}+2x){|}_{-4}^{0}\\,+\\,(-{x}^{2}+x){|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{4}{0}^{2}+2(0)-(\\frac{1}{4}(-4)^{2}+2(-4))]\\,+\\,[-{3}^{2}+3-(-{0}^{2}+0)] \\\\  & =[\\,0-(4-8)]\\,+\\,[\\,-9+3-0] \\\\  & =4-6 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342008/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec980fcb-97ed-5c60-94de-0521d9d7df27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342008"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117702/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "1adc9afb-e7c0-5fdd-a4d3-c3dd940dc26b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117702/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "b683bc48-e786-553b-b5a2-9cff7eb61c5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117702/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "abf7b063-ee50-5728-ad99-832cfe7442cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117702/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "682b381d-5e6e-5160-94ad-9d4a8ed756e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117702/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "650bc56e-d4be-56f7-9782-82bca026b5e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117702/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "656e0866-f42a-5d57-9e9d-258ff950f4fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117702/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-117702/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-117702/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-117702/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-117702/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-117702/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117702" :question/id #uuid "5e1ef3f5-5fb9-5108-bf98-1048434bd777" :question/math-academy-id "q-117702" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036389/assets/f725b571954587b7b88426a254d7a6fc05f09b63ab2cc94b81303a510e8c1798.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of two line segments. Find the value of ${\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We divide the interval of integration into $3$ regions: the line segment for $x\\in [-2,0],$ the line segment for $x\\in [0,2),$ and the line segment for $x\\in [2,3].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-2}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-2,0].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,2).$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [2,3].$ The corresponding region is a rectangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =bh \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2}+{A}_{3} \\\\  & =2-2+2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117702/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4abe11e-febf-5461-96ee-bca8a7713bdf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117702"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49168/selection/e444404dc07367ac8016bda434c10eb523081870436c295516fac19414429c5c" :answer/id #uuid "04f30b91-a338-580d-9c54-07e93c40c717" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49168/selection/cadf76b3c9ea81d49a7c0215bbafd960b57c9361c98f1ffb78838a079e98a76e" :answer/id #uuid "4b2a525b-4544-56f6-a730-d5d8ebd065b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49168/selection/4e9045bda7c91382ad1f9e6db34ef05a3d44373a1af992c86cb541161e72c24f" :answer/id #uuid "015a1ea7-f5d8-58d7-93cd-6453d6e9c5cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49168/selection/ab3343a580c9ecbbb4e27d0c43b67b7d3815a6806a811b62927c9243c7c87034" :answer/id #uuid "8aee7257-7e21-5a3b-9509-4909fc0ba609" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49168/selection/d0d01bb2e3e816b9fd6aee47accd74e6df07f3f36fe536db4d7bfbcde2546d68" :answer/id #uuid "d942adeb-6f59-5783-a155-0f35a476c34c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49168/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b88d8800-3dae-550c-b54f-1cdc36e62d64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49168/selection/4e9045bda7c91382ad1f9e6db34ef05a3d44373a1af992c86cb541161e72c24f" :answer-field/choices ["q-49168/selection/e444404dc07367ac8016bda434c10eb523081870436c295516fac19414429c5c" "q-49168/selection/cadf76b3c9ea81d49a7c0215bbafd960b57c9361c98f1ffb78838a079e98a76e" "q-49168/selection/4e9045bda7c91382ad1f9e6db34ef05a3d44373a1af992c86cb541161e72c24f" "q-49168/selection/ab3343a580c9ecbbb4e27d0c43b67b7d3815a6806a811b62927c9243c7c87034" "q-49168/selection/d0d01bb2e3e816b9fd6aee47accd74e6df07f3f36fe536db4d7bfbcde2546d68"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49168" :question/id #uuid "9e3aa613-866d-5cee-a63d-5bfb35b4f81e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49168" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036389/assets/96622ea1476cf79ec3ff6d6486d77eda465de80d005304f542b4aadfb6be2b7a.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of two line segments. Find the value of ${\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of two parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-3,0]$ and the line segment for $x\\in (0,4].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-3}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-3,0].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =4.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (0,4].$ The corresponding region is a rectangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =ab \\\\  & =2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-8.\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4.5-8 \\\\  & =-3.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-49168/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4abe11e-febf-5461-96ee-bca8a7713bdf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49168"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-86167"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Acad